# A way Muldrotha gives is a permission, so a card cast by it may be cast for an alternative cost of its own instead of its mana
# cost (the ruling, CR 118.9, 601.3). Thought Scour mills Overlord of the Hauntwoods and Elvish Mystic. On turn 3 Bot1 casts the
# Mystic through the creature way, so the Overlord (an enchantment creature) is left only the enchantment way, and casts it through
# that for its impending cost {1}{G}{G} (CR 702.176a): it enters with four time counters, not a creature, and makes its Everywhere
# land token.

